[26.992578, "o", "\r\n================ FINAL ================\r\n\r\nDiagnosis, Evidence, Action taken, Result.\r\n\r\nThe initial step test (ds1) showed oscillation and overshoot, indicating the controller was too aggressive. The analysis suggested reducing the proportional and integral gains. After applying the proposed PID gains (ds2), the oscillation has stopped, the overshoot is reduced to 0.65%, and the system has settled within the expected range.\r\n\r\nEvidences:\r\n- Oscillation in ds1: \"error(setpoint-pv) [1.38s to 27.50s]: decay_ratio = 1.002 (threshold 0.5)\", \"error(setpoint-pv) [1.38s to 27.50s]: period = 1.58s\", \"error(setpoint-pv) [1.38s to 27.50s]: last_amplitude = 0.1298 (threshold 0.02)\", \"error(setpoint-pv) [1.38s to 27.50s]: cycles = 17 (threshold 3)\".\r\n- Reduced oscillation in ds2: \"oscillating\": false, \"settling_time_s\": 4.3, \"settled\": true.\r\n\r\nAction taken: The PID gains were adjusted from (4.0, 1.5, 0.0) to (1.8182, 0.5231, 0.456), as suggested by the analysis.\r\n\r\nResult: The system is now stable with reduced overshoot and settled within the expected range.\r\n"]
[27.249886, "o", "\r\nSaved results/results.md, results/pid_before_after.png, results/audit_log.json\r\n"]
